  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Summary",
      "html": "<p>This optional unit adds 50 words that occur 17–19 times in the New Testament and are not in Machen&#x27;s lessons: 24 nouns, 14 verbs and 12 other words. Nothing in the course waits for them; they are here so that you can read the New Testament with the lexicon open less often. Learn them on the Words track: recognize, recall, type, type with accents.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Built from words you know",
      "html": "<p>These verbs are a preposition plus a verb from the lessons; the meaning usually follows from the parts: παρατίθημι (τίθημι); εἰσπορεύομαι (πορεύομαι); ἐπιβάλλω (βάλλω); προστίθημι (τίθημι).</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Common confusion",
      "html": "<p>Look-alikes that differ by one letter: κτίσις (creation) and κρίσις (a judgment); πότε (when) and τότε (then); τέλειος (perfect) and τελειόω (I complete); ἀληθῶς (truly) and ἀληθής (true); κενός (empty) and γένος (a race); κόπος (trouble) and τόπος (a place); φανερός (apparent) and φανερόω (I make manifest).</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Source",
      "html": "<p>Words chosen by their New Testament frequency (MorphGNT); glosses after Jeffrey Dodson&#x27;s Greek-English lexicon (public domain).</p>"
    },
